From 3d612cd3053f50a875f2f668bd05a5b99b7683cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dcasati <dcasati@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:01:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] ath12k.4: add manual page

Document the LinuxKPI-based ath12k driver for the Qualcomm WCN7850,
following the layout of rtw88.4 and rtw89.4: loading, the firmware
package, the ath12k_wifi7N device name, station mode and strict
regulatory behavior, the hw.ath12k.country and LinuxKPI module
parameter tunables, and the current limits.  List ath12k in
linuxkpi_wlan.4.

Like ath10k.4, the page is not yet hooked up in man4/Makefile, as the
module is not built from sys/modules/Makefile.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 share/man/man4/ath12k.4        | 156 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 share/man/man4/linuxkpi_wlan.4 |   2 +
 2 files changed, 158 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 share/man/man4/ath12k.4

diff --git a/share/man/man4/ath12k.4 b/share/man/man4/ath12k.4
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..657c90f7524
--- /dev/null
+++ b/share/man/man4/ath12k.4
@@ -0,0 +1,156 @@
+.\"
+.\" Copyright (c) 2026 Diego Casati <diego.casati@gmail.com>
+.\"
+.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
+.\"
+.Dd October 26, 2026
+.Dt ATH12K 4
+.Os
+.Sh NAME
+.Nm ath12k
+.Nd Qualcomm IEEE 802.11be wireless network driver
+.Sh SYNOPSIS
+The driver will auto-load without any user interaction using
+.Xr devmatch 8
+if enabled in
+.Xr rc.conf 5 .
+.Pp
+Only if auto-loading is explicitly disabled, place the following
+lines in
+.Xr rc.conf 5
+to manually load the driver as a module at boot time:
+.Bd -literal -offset indent
+kld_list="${kld_list} if_ath12k"
+.Ed
+.Pp
+It is discouraged to load the driver from
+.Xr loader 8 .
+.Sh DESCRIPTION
+The
+.Nm
+driver is derived from Qualcomm's Linux ath12k driver
+based on Linux version 7.0.
+.Pp
+This driver requires firmware to be loaded before it will work.
+The package
+.Pa wifi-firmware-ath12k-kmod
+from the
+.Pa ports/net/wifi-firmware-ath12k-kmod
+port needs to be installed before the driver is loaded.
+Otherwise no
+.Xr wlan 4
+interface can be created using
+.Xr ifconfig 8 .
+One can use
+.Xr fwget 8
+to install the correct firmware package.
+.Pp
+The driver uses the
+.Xr linuxkpi_wlan 4
+and
+.Xr linuxkpi 4
+compat framework to bridge between the Linux and
+native
+.Fx
+driver code as well as to the native
+.Xr net80211 4
+wireless stack.
+The MHI bus and the QMI messaging support needed by
+.Nm
+are implemented in
+.Xr linuxkpi 4 .
+.Pp
+The device attaches as
+.Li ath12k_wifi7 Ns Ar N .
+Only station mode is supported.
+A
+.Xr wlan 4
+interface is created with:
+.Bd -literal -offset indent
+ifconfig wlan0 create wlandev ath12k_wifi70
+.Ed
+.Pp
+The driver applies strict regulatory rules.
+Channels which the regulatory domain marks as
+.Dq no initiating radiation
+or as requiring DFS are scanned passively only.
+The regulatory country cannot be changed at runtime;
+see
+.Va hw.ath12k.country
+below.
+.Sh HARDWARE
+The
+.Nm
+driver supports PCIe devices with the following chipsets:
+.Pp
+.Bl -bullet -offset indent -compact
+.It
+Qualcomm WCN7850 hw2.0
+.El
+.Pp
+The driver also matches the Qualcomm QCN9274 and QCC2072 PCI IDs,
+but only the WCN7850 has been tested on
+.Fx .
+.Sh LOADER TUNABLES
+Tunables can be set in
+.Xr loader.conf 5
+and are read when the module is loaded.
+.Bl -tag -width indent
+.It Va hw.ath12k.country
+ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code, in upper case, for example
+.Ql CA .
+The driver requests this regulatory country from the firmware before
+the boot-time regulatory domain is published.
+If unset or not two upper case letters, the regulatory domain
+reported by the firmware is used.
+The default is unset.
+.It Va compat.linuxkpi.ath12k_core_debug_mask
+Bitmask of driver debug messages to enable.
+This is also a read-write
+.Xr sysctl 8
+variable.
+The default is 0.
+.It Va compat.linuxkpi.ath12k_core_ftm_mode
+Boot the firmware in factory test mode.
+This is not intended for normal operation.
+The default is 0.
+.El
+.Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr linuxkpi 4 ,
+.Xr linuxkpi_wlan 4 ,
+.Xr net80211 4 ,
+.Xr wlan 4 ,
+.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
+.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
+.Xr networking 7 ,
+.Xr devmatch 8 ,
+.Xr fwget 8 ,
+.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
+.Xr wpa_supplicant 8
+.Sh HISTORY
+.\" XXX Review: confirm the release before committing upstream.
+The
+.Nm
+driver first appeared in
+.Fx 16.0 .
+.Sh CAVEATS
+The
+.Va wlans_ Ns Ar parent
+variable in
+.Xr rc.conf 5
+does not accept parent device names containing an underscore,
+so the
+.Xr wlan 4
+interface for
+.Li ath12k_wifi70
+has to be created explicitly with
+.Xr ifconfig 8 .
+.Sh BUGS
+While
+.Nm
+supports 802.11a/b/g/n/ac/ax/be modes,
+the compatibility code currently only supports 802.11a/b/g/n/ac modes.
+802.11ax/be, multi-link operation (MLO), 160 MHz channels and
+the 6 GHz band are not supported.
+.Pp
+Host AP mode is not supported and monitor mode has not been tested.
diff --git a/share/man/man4/linuxkpi_wlan.4 b/share/man/man4/linuxkpi_wlan.4
index fa0b15b5e0b..358ccc16398 100644
--- a/share/man/man4/linuxkpi_wlan.4
+++ b/share/man/man4/linuxkpi_wlan.4
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@ support, it was decided not to do so given
 has been deprecated since 2004.
 .Pp
 The list of supported drivers includes
+.Xr ath12k 4 ,
 .Xr iwlwifi 4 ,
 .Xr rtw88 4 ,
 and
@@ -127,6 +128,7 @@ This sysctl is
 and normally only needed for debugging purposes.
 .El
 .Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr ath12k 4 ,
 .Xr iwlwifi 4 ,
 .Xr linuxkpi 4 ,
 .Xr rtw88 4 ,
